@* The whole document a dead request answers with, and not just the face: the request never
   reached the app's own root component, so nothing else is going to emit the shell the face
   is styled by. Same NsApp chrome and same NsAssets the app's own root composes, so the page
   a reader lands on here looks like the app they were already in. *@
<NsApp>
    <Head>
        <NsAssets />
    </Head>
    <Body>
        @* The face reads its colours off --mud-palette-*, which the vendor stylesheet leaves
           unset: under the layout NsSetup has already mounted the theme, and here nothing has,
           so the document mounts it itself. No brand was resolved -- the request died before
           anything could -- so NsTheme paints its neutral grey. *@
        <NsTheme />
        <NsPageError HomePage="@HomePage" Handle="@Handle" />
    </Body>
</NsApp>

@code {

    /// <summary>The page mounted at the app's root, where the door back leads — read off the
    /// route table by whoever renders this, never written.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Type? HomePage { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The request's own trace id, the reference a report is filed by.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Handle { get; set; }
}
